Reading a fence turns a null value into the string <null>.

Yams reads `published:` as NSNull. Frontmatter.normalizeForYAML tests
for Bool, Int, Double and String, and NSNull matches none of them, so
it falls through to "\(value)" and becomes the six character string
<null>. Yams then emits that string as a plain scalar.

The value stops being null and becomes text. With --set -i the same
path writes <null> into the user's file, so a null the user wrote is
lost the first time any key is set.

normalizeForYAML should pass NSNull through so Yams emits `null`.
